{"name":"Keel Joy","hex":"#d49595","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"keel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large beam along the underside of a ship’s hull from bow to stern.","A rigid, flat piece of material anchored to the lowest part of the hull of a ship to give it greater control and stability."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To collapse, to fall.","To traverse with a keel; to navigate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/keel"},{"term":"joy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A feeling of extreme happiness or cheerfulness, especially related to the acquisition or expectation of something good.","Anything that causes such a feeling."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Expressing appreciation and happiness."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/joy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Keel","blocks":[{"text":"The keel is the bottom-most longitudinal structural element of a watercraft, important for stability. On some sailboats, it may have a hydrodynamic and counterbalancing purpose as well. The laying of the keel is often the initial step in constructing a ship. In the British and American shipbuilding traditions, this event marks the beginning date of a ship's construction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/The_keel_plate_of_USS_United_States_%28CVA-58%29_being_laid_in_a_construction_dry_dock_on_18_April_1948.jpg/330px-The_keel_plate_of_USS_United_States_%28CVA-58%29_being_laid_in_a_construction_dry_dock_on_18_April_1948.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keel","wikidata":"Q582062"},{"title":"Joy","blocks":[{"text":"Joy is the state of being that allows one to experience feelings of intense, long-lasting happiness and contentment of life. It is closely related to, and often evoked by, well-being, success, or good fortune. Happiness, pleasure, and gratitude are closely related to joy but are not identical to it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/A_Smiling_boy_from_Bangladesh.jpg/330px-A_Smiling_boy_from_Bangladesh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joy","wikidata":"Q935526"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/MariahQuarterView.jpg/500px-MariahQuarterView.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/MariahQuarterView.jpg/1280px-MariahQuarterView.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/MariahQuarterView.jpg/500px-MariahQuarterView.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sailing yacht with a fin keel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMariahQuarterView.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Sara_Ahmed-IMG_6457.jpg/500px-Sara_Ahmed-IMG_6457.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Sara_Ahmed-IMG_6457.jpg/1280px-Sara_Ahmed-IMG_6457.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Sara_Ahmed-IMG_6457.jpg/500px-Sara_Ahmed-IMG_6457.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Scholar Sara Ahmed introduced the concept of joy as a \"sticky\" emotion","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASara_Ahmed-IMG_6457.jpg"}],"sounds":{"keel":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/32/En-us-keel.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/32/